The `runAttachServable` stub: for `release view` with ANY `--json*` it echoes "SHA256SUMS" — the gate's combined probe gets the literal string "SHA256SUMS" → invalid JSON → jq fails → fail-closed refusal → exit 1 → the flip never runs → test fails.

This stub needs a structured answer for the combined probe. The scenario: release exists as a DRAFT carrying SHA256SUMS (the recovery-flip path being tested). So: `--json isDraft,assets` → `{"isDraft":true,"assets":[{"name":"a.zip"},{"name":"SHA256SUMS"}]}` and `--json isDraft` (flip check) → "true", `--json assets` → "SHA256SUMS" (the servability probe expects the NAMES list). Update the stub:

``
   view)
     case "$*" in
       *--json\ isDraft,assets*) echo '{"isDraft":true,"assets":[{"name":"a.zip"},{"name":"SHA256SUMS"}]}'; exit 0 ;;
       *--json\ isDraft*) echo "true"; exit 0 ;;
       *--json*) echo "SHA256SUMS" ;;
     esac
     exit 0 ;;
``

In the Dart string, escape: `\$` for bash vars — none here. The `{}` are fine.

